      "content": "Reducing the dosage or frequency of vitamin K might minimize interactions with warfarin, but it's always best to consult with your doctor before making any adjustments. They can help determine a tailored approach for your individual situation and may recommend alternative, more precise ways to manage your bone health, such as supplements or medication. Your doctor may also be willing to space out your blood tests more frequently to account for your more conservative vitamin K routine.",
